# ---- Storage ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Postgres connection string, e.g. Supabase (required on Vercel). Leave unset to use a local file.
# Supabase: Project › Connect › "Transaction pooler" (port 6543), with your database password filled in.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres
# Local file location when DATABASE_URL isn't set (default ./data/cv-tailor.db).
# DATABASE_PATH=./data/cv-tailor.db

# ---- Sign-in (required when deployed) --------------------------------------
# People sign in with Google, or with an email and a password set through a one-time
# link the owner makes. Only OWNER_EMAIL and the emails the owner approves get in, and
# each gets their own data. Without the Google settings, the app only runs locally,
# open to this computer. See "Deploy to Vercel" in the README.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Signs sign-in cookies. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# SESSION_SECRET=
# Your email: always allowed in, and approves everyone else.
# OWNER_EMAIL=

# Optional extra MCP key. With sign-in it works as the owner's key; locally it guards
# the MCP endpoint (needed for tunnels). Generate with: openssl rand -hex 24
# MCP_TOKEN=

# Address of the web app, used in links your chat receives.
# Defaults to Vercel's production address on Vercel, else http://localhost:3000.
# APP_URL=

# ---- Optional AI ------------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed: your chat app does the writing. With a key, a pasted job
# description gets a better first-pass read before your chat refines it.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5
